WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.344 --> 00:00:04.685
- Hi, I'm Lenny Lipton;
this is my dog Belle.

00:00:04.685 --> 00:00:07.725
- [Narrator] Lenny Lipton is
sitting in his living room.

00:00:07.725 --> 00:00:10.291
- [Lenny] Puff the Magic Dragon

00:00:10.291 --> 00:00:12.746
- [Narrator] Reading something
you've probably heard.

00:00:12.746 --> 00:00:15.109
- [Lenny] Lived by the sea and
frolicked in the autumn mist

00:00:15.109 --> 00:00:17.008
in a land called Honalee.

00:00:17.008 --> 00:00:19.173
♫ Puff the Magic Dragon

00:00:19.173 --> 00:00:20.890
- [Narrator] Lenny wrote what has

00:00:20.890 --> 00:00:22.064
become the stoner's anthem.

00:00:22.064 --> 00:00:23.333
- [Lenny] I wrote Puff the Magic Dragon.

00:00:23.333 --> 00:00:25.189
- [Narrator] When he was a
19-year-old college student.

00:00:25.189 --> 00:00:27.173
- [Lenny] I was a freshman at Cornell.

00:00:27.173 --> 00:00:28.378
Belle can you sit?

00:00:28.378 --> 00:00:29.626
Thank you dear.

00:00:29.626 --> 00:00:33.360
Okay, I was reading a poem by Ogden Nash

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:35.781
called Custard the Dragon.

00:00:35.781 --> 00:00:38.330
- [Narrator] Soon after he went
to meet friends for dinner.

00:00:38.330 --> 00:00:41.776
- [Lenny] As I was walking
down the hill to the apartment,

00:00:41.776 --> 00:00:43.781
I was thinking about the poem I read,

00:00:43.781 --> 00:00:46.754
and I thought I'd try to
write one too, about a dragon.

00:00:46.754 --> 00:00:48.439
- [Narrator] He got to
his friend's apartment

00:00:48.439 --> 00:00:49.900
and let himself in.

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:53.292
- [Lenny] I saw a typewriter
on a kitchen table,

00:00:53.292 --> 00:00:56.407
and I typed "Puff the Magic
Dragon lived by the sea

00:00:56.407 --> 00:01:00.076
and frolicked in the autumn
mist in a land called Honalee."

00:01:00.076 --> 00:01:02.199
And although I didn't find out about

00:01:02.199 --> 00:01:03.394
this for a couple years,

00:01:03.394 --> 00:01:06.066
Peter Yarrow, who became the
Peter of Peter, Paul and Mary,

00:01:06.066 --> 00:01:08.210
was one of the guys who
lived in the apartment.

00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:09.320
He saved the poem.

00:01:09.320 --> 00:01:10.770
I completely forgot about it.

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:12.189
I even left it in the typewriter,

00:01:12.189 --> 00:01:13.714
and he set it to music.

00:01:13.714 --> 00:01:16.530
That's how the song got
written and it changed my life.

00:01:16.530 --> 00:01:20.381
(upbeat ukulele music)

00:01:20.381 --> 00:01:22.845
- [Narrator] But Lenny's
story doesn't stop there.

00:01:22.845 --> 00:01:25.096
- [Lenny] I've got
something like 72 patents.

00:01:25.096 --> 00:01:27.549
I invented the way to project 3-D movies,

00:01:27.549 --> 00:01:29.800
you're likely to see if
you go to the cinemas.

00:01:29.800 --> 00:01:32.210
- [Narrator] He also invented
those awkward glasses

00:01:32.210 --> 00:01:34.013
you have to wear to see them.

00:01:34.013 --> 00:01:38.079
- This is crystallized, this
is the first commercial pair

00:01:38.079 --> 00:01:40.746
of 3-D active electronic eyewear.

00:01:42.068 --> 00:01:43.850
- [Narrator] And everyone from NASA

00:01:43.850 --> 00:01:45.608
to James Cameron has used them.

00:01:45.608 --> 00:01:48.125
- NASA on Mars and Cameron underwater.

00:01:48.125 --> 00:01:49.981
- [Narrator] Lenny is also a filmmaker.

00:01:49.981 --> 00:01:51.869
He's produced over 25 movies.

00:01:51.869 --> 00:01:53.842
- It's a lifetime achievement award.

00:01:53.842 --> 00:01:56.146
- [Narrator] And he's written
several books all about,

00:01:56.146 --> 00:01:58.237
well, film and one autobiography.

00:01:58.237 --> 00:02:00.829
- But I don't think it's of interest.

00:02:00.829 --> 00:02:02.395
My wife read one chapter

00:02:02.395 --> 00:02:04.112
and she said she didn't
want to read any more.

00:02:04.112 --> 00:02:05.128
(Lenny laughs)

00:02:05.128 --> 00:02:06.660
- [Narrator] Okay, so
a book about his life

00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:08.174
is not his magnum opus.

00:02:08.174 --> 00:02:10.308
Good thing a song about drugs is,

00:02:10.308 --> 00:02:12.676
cause that's what it's about, right?

00:02:12.676 --> 00:02:14.723
- If people want to think it's about pot,

00:02:14.723 --> 00:02:17.027
that's fine with me.

00:02:17.027 --> 00:02:18.435
- [Narrator] Wait, it's not?

00:02:18.435 --> 00:02:20.035
- Not as far as I'm concerned.

00:02:20.035 --> 00:02:21.586
Puff the Magic Dragon is not about drugs,

00:02:21.586 --> 00:02:23.114
and who knows, who knows what I was thinking?

00:02:23.114 --> 00:02:27.197
♫ Lives in a land called Honalee

